QUALITY TARGET
Write for actual literary quality, not for a numeric emotion target. Prefer precise, coherent, memorable language over generic poetic atmosphere. Avoid vague profundity, adjective stacking, strained metaphors, and automatic filler such as "ancient", "forgotten", "shadow", "sorrow", or "whisper" unless the specific sentence truly needs them.

